 "_note": "Per-character voice sets read by native/src/audio/sfx.rs. Each action maps to layers [name, variants]: a name from sounds.json plays through the SM64 sound engine; a name starting with voices/ is a ROM-extracted clip, assets/audio/<name>_<i>.wav for i < variants, one picked at random (scripts/export-character-voices.py: Link and young Link from Ocarina of Time NA_SE_VO_LI_*, Banjo and Kazooie from Banjo-Kazooie sfx_e). Bowser, a skin on Mario, uses SM64's own Bowser effects from the sound bank (laugh, fire, defeat). The Smash fighters (ids ssb-*) each have a set ssb_<fighter> of SSB64 voices and effects rendered from the user's ROM by the Smash import (scripts/export-ssb64-sounds.py, native/byor-rs/src/ssb64_sounds.rs) into assets/audio/voices/ssb64/; those sets are native/src/characters/smash_audio.rs VOICE_KEYS applied to its table (a test keeps them equal), including MARIO_PUNCH_YAH/WAH/HOO and MARIO_HRMM, Mario voices a non-Mario set may answer by name. The old shared id ssb64 stays silent. Actions with no fitting sample stay empty; clips missing from a build without that ROM are silent. Non-voice effects (footsteps, landing, swim, coin...) are not character specific and stay in Sfx. Mario's SM64 voice clips may only appear in the mario set. MENU_STAR_SOUND is a jingle, not a voice.",
